{"id": "c06d7d30-dae8-499e-a0d9-89b9d91558fd", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The AD directory is active and healthy with matching DNS IPs, so the join failure must be internal—likely a service account or OU issue. I should pull the ontapErrorMessage from the two UpdateStorageVirtualMachine events on Nov 2, and note the workload shows zero client ops over the past 7 days, consistent with this being a test environment.

Volume provisioning also looks fine—vol_nfs at 200 GiB and vol_smb at 50 GiB total well within the 861 GiB usable capacity, so thin provisioning isn't the bottleneck. With no I/O baseline to work from, I can't predict batch performance, so I need to check the per-volume utilization, the full UpdateSVM events, network configuration (security groups, route tables, NACLs, ENIs), and snapshot details to rule out other causes.

